x86_64-linux  two divergences, both already recorded. A class template specialization is spelled without the namespace it was declared in - cxx1 writes ?most@?$Bounds@H@@ where clang writes ?most@?$Bounds@H@lim@@, and _ZN3lim... likewise - because templates are keyed by their bare name and a specialization does not know which namespace it came from; docs/CONFORMANCE.md records that and what fixing it costs. And on Itanium a member function template's name encodes the pattern signature, VecIXT_EE, where cxx1 writes the substituted VecILi3EE - the same split template-member.nonames records, needing the pattern carried through the member-template mangler. What this case is about, a namespace-qualified template-id as a qualifier and a deduced member template, is checked by run.sh on all three machines.
